(1136879, 140579, 16106, '<td valign="top">i find the gaussian blur a bit heavy handed here. If you are trying to simulate a narrow DOF having one plane in focus rather than one part of one plane. A layered blurr that gets stronger as it moves away from the focus point rather then a binary sharp / blurred line is more appealing.</td>', 'i find the gaussian blur a bit heavy handed here. If you are trying to simulate a narrow DOF having one plane in focus rather than one part of one plane. A layered blurr that gets stronger as it moves away from the focus point rather then a binary sharp / blurred line is more appealing.', '2005-01-28 11:05:50.000000', NULL, 1),
(1136883, 140347, 7263, '<td valign="top">Very nice idea, but you''ll probably get ripped apart by the voters :(<br/> <br/>Also, the last 2 look like a 3 on it''s side! Accidental or very clever!</td>', 'Very nice idea, but you''ll probably get ripped apart by the voters :( Also, the last 2 look like a 3 on it''s side! Accidental or very clever!', '2005-01-28 11:08:14.000000', NULL, 1),
