(1150295, 140491, 19010, '<td valign="top">Greetings From the Critique Club!!!<br/> <br/>Initial Impact: Not very lively<br/> <br/>Does it Fit the Challenge: Without a doubt. You not only met it once but twice. That a bit of a treat for us viewers.<br/> <br/>Focus: The focus is good in this shot. The birds the water and the posts all seem to be in focus. To be honest I can''t even find the point of focus (not that thats a bad thing)<br/> <br/>Color: I feel that this is to pretty a shot to have such melow colors. I feel this shot would have done a world better if it were brighter and had more vibrrant colors. <br/> <br/>Composition: The composition looks pretty good and works as is. I am however wondering if by cropping a little of the water off the top and bottom would help pop the subject into the spotlight a little better. I also feel a little border could have helped.<br/> <br/>Overall: I feel this has the potential to be a spectacular shot. With just a little playing around with the levels and a little cop. I think this was a good shhot the just scored low because to me it looks unfinished. If you do decide to play around with the few sugestions I had I would absolutaly love to see the finished product.</td>', 'Greetings From the Critique Club!!! Initial Impact: Not very lively Does it Fit the Challenge: Without a doubt. You not only met it once but twice. That a bit of a treat for us viewers. Focus: The focus is good in this shot. The birds the water and the posts all seem to be in focus. To be honest I can''t even find the point of focus (not that thats a bad thing) Color: I feel that this is to pretty a shot to have such melow colors. I feel this shot would have done a world better if it were brighter and had more vibrrant colors.  Composition: The composition looks pretty good and works as is. I am however wondering if by cropping a little of the water off the top and bottom would help pop the subject into the spotlight a little better. I also feel a little border could have helped. Overall: I feel this has the potential to be a spectacular shot. With just a little playing around with the levels and a little cop. I think this was a good shhot the just scored low because to me it looks unfinished. If you do decide to play around with the few sugestions I had I would absolutaly love to see the finished product.', '2005-02-04 08:46:18.000000', NULL, 0),
(1150300, 140094, 255, '<td valign="top"><table align="center" width="95%"><tr><td><div class="textsm"><b>Originally posted by goodman:</b></div><hr/><i> <br/>[i prefer doris] :) </i></td></tr></table> <br/>uh huh. ;)</td>', 'Originally posted by goodman: [i prefer doris] :)  uh huh. ;)', '2005-02-04 08:53:02.000000', NULL, 0),
(1150305, 140583, 12253, '<td valign="top">I like the geometry here, and like the lighting in the back as it plays off the curves. I see two things that might have made it better to me:<br/> <br/>1) Crop the right, it seems unbalanced past the tree. I suggest just to the right of the right edge of the main tree that''s lit on the left. That puts the tree towards the upper right corner, and the arcs more or less defining the bottom left corner. Some balance.<br/> <br/>2) Consider cloning out the white reflectors in the road.</td>', 'I like the geometry here, and like the lighting in the back as it plays off the curves. I see two things that might have made it better to me: 1) Crop the right, it seems unbalanced past the tree. I suggest just to the right of the right edge of the main tree that''s lit on the left. That puts the tree towards the upper right corner, and the arcs more or less defining the bottom left corner. Some balance. 2) Consider cloning out the white reflectors in the road.', '2005-02-04 08:59:15.000000', NULL, 0),
