(1150779, 140240, 24976, '<td valign="top"><table align="center" width="95%"><tr><td><div class="textsm"><b>Originally posted by sgauria:</b></div><hr/><i> Congrats.<br/>Can you explain what part of the body this is.<br/>Just want to understand how this was done.<br/> <br/>Thanks </i></td></tr></table> <br/> <br/>Its the neck, shoulder and part of the chin. The head is tilted back and angled away so it gave that part a really wierd shape, so imagine the chin now is pointing into the page towards the top right and you dont really see it. Plus the shoulders were sort of in a shrug gesture making the neck appear shorter, and plus the shadows distorted the shapes even further... I cant say i planned it exactly like this, it just sorta happened :-)<br/>Lighting came from one table lamp. I had a this and a color version but decided this had more punch to it.<br/><br/><i>Message edited by author 2005-02-04 15:33:30.</i></td>', 'Originally posted by sgauria: Congrats.Can you explain what part of the body this is.Just want to understand how this was done. Thanks   Its the neck, shoulder and part of the chin. The head is tilted back and angled away so it gave that part a really wierd shape, so imagine the chin now is pointing into the page towards the top right and you dont really see it. Plus the shoulders were sort of in a shrug gesture making the neck appear shorter, and plus the shadows distorted the shapes even further... I cant say i planned it exactly like this, it just sorta happened :-)Lighting came from one table lamp. I had a this and a color version but decided this had more punch to it.', '2005-02-04 15:32:12.000000', '2005-02-04 15:33:30.000000', 0),
